<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46928" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭpīnĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		supinus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a bending backwards</i> (very rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">est odiosa omnis supinitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3, 122</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Planasia (insula) de supinitate sic vocata,</span>”
				<i>its lying flat</i>, <i>flatness</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sol. 3, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
